id: pm-a5w7vv
title: "As an operator, I can ask pm a question in plain prose and receive the exact structured query plus its bounded answer, so insight never requires memorizing the flag grammar"
description: "Exploration story (spike + ADR only). Natural-language intent compilation: map a prose question ('what blocked the release last week', 'which items has this agent touched') onto the structured query surface (list/search/graph filters) with the compiled query always shown, deterministic, and inspectable. The compiled query is the product: NL is an input convenience, never a hidden second query engine. Acceptance of any implementation slice is measured by the retrieval quality contract (pm-p1g43q), not by prose plausibility. Horizon: far (4+), after the grammar freeze (pm-agou) so the compilation target is stable."
type: Story
status: open
priority: 4
